---
import Legal from '../../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site } from '../../site';
const subject = encodeURIComponent('Delete my Escaque account');
const body = encodeURIComponent('Hello,\n\nI want to delete my Escaque account.\n\nUsername: @\nAccount email: \n');
---
<Legal lang="en" title="Delete your Escaque account" description="How to delete your Escaque account and what data is deleted.">
  <h2>From the app (immediately)</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Open Escaque and go to <strong>Settings → Account</strong>.</li>
    <li>Tap <strong>Delete account</strong> and confirm. We may ask for your password or to sign in with Google again.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Without the app</h2>
  <p>Write to us from your account’s email address:</p>
  <p><a class="btn btn-primary" href={`mailto:${site.email}?subject=${subject}&body=${body}`}>Request deletion by email</a></p>
  <p class="muted">To protect your account, we only handle requests sent from the email you signed up with. We will complete it within 30 days and confirm by email.</p>

  <h2>What is deleted</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Your sign-in account (email and sign-in method).</li>
    <li>Your profile, your notification preferences and your devices’ notification tokens.</li>
    <li>Your username, which becomes available to others.</li>
    <li>Your friendships, requests and blocks, and your rating (you leave the leaderboards at their next update).</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>What happens to your games</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Ongoing online games end and your opponent wins.</li>
    <li>Games waiting for an opponent are cancelled.</li>
    <li>In finished games your name is replaced by “Deleted account” so your opponents keep their history.</li>
    <li>Games saved on your phone without an account were never sent to us: they stay on your device until you uninstall the app.</li>
  </ul>
</Legal>
